{{also|Apsis|āpsis}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|la|apsis}}, {{m|la|hapsis}}, from {{der|en|grc|ἁψίς||arch, vault}}. See also {{m|en|apse}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈæpsɪs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|apsides}}

# {{lb|en|architecture}} A [[recess]] or [[projection]], with a [[dome]] or [[vault]], at the [[east]] end of a [[church]]; an [[apse]].
# {{lb|en|astronomy}} Either of the [[point]]s in the [[elliptical]] [[orbit]] of a [[planet]] or [[comet]] where it is [[closest]] or [[furthest]] from the [[sun]]; [[perihelion]] or [[aphelion]]; an [[apside]]

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|periapsis}}
* {{l|en|apoapsis}}

